// Per the D2 row: a per-language `data <lang>_<prim>:
// OrderedRing<<lang>Prim, …>` inhabitance is the parallel-substrate
// INVARIANTS P1:42 forbids (`numeric_aliases_align_to_refinements`)
// — superseded. The prior #3174 head's RustScalar Disj REGISTRY
// (18 named `data rust_X: RustScalar = …` rows) + IrToRust<IRCarrier>
// carrier + bool_to_rust_bool row + assert_bool_to_rust_bool_consistency
// fn DISSOLVE into the three-thin-facts shape (this commit). The
// faithful RustScalar TYPE vocabulary (the Disj of source-syntax
// scalar categories with payload-bearing variants — IntScalar /
// FloatScalar / BoolScalar / CharScalar / StrScalar / NeverScalar —
// declared above) STAYS as the parse-stage source-syntax
// classifier; only the inhabitance-form items dissolve.
//
// Per the D2 row's D2.2: coercion = the U1 homomorphism realized by
// the generic B2-OMNI emit fold reading the resolver data. NOT a
// hand table (the prior IrToRust<> per-target string table is the
// shape INVARIANTS P1 forbids — its dissolution is exactly this
// reshape). NOT a per-language emit lens (B2-OMNI/B4: one generic
// emit, target-specificity is declarative T-11 data).
//
// Per the D2 row's D2.3: compound/generic coercion composes for
// FREE via the Node catamorphism (A1's single recursive type;
// `List<Int32>` = `Instantiation` recursed); no per-instantiation
// rows. Not blocked on the Functor hierarchy.
//
// Per the D2 row's D2.4: round-trip guarantee is structural-on-F
// per C5-1; TestClaims document it, never establish it. The prior
// Layer-2 `assert_bool_to_rust_bool_consistency` fn — a forward-
// anchor that documented an assertion the structural law makes
// redundant — dissolves with this commit.
